From 937b8ef693c4a4eb9cd5077b665b9af224db8607 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:35:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: use V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE, not the
 buf_type enumerator

probe picked vfl_dir with

    else if (vd->device_caps &
             (V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_OUTPUT | V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE))

where the second constant is a BUFFER TYPE whose value is 10, not a
capability bit. The test therefore read `caps & (0x2 | 0xa)`: it
matched V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_OUTPUT (0x2) and the unassigned bit 0x8, and it
never matched V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE (0x2000).

An output-MPLANE-only device thus fell through to VFL_DIR_RX, and
v4l2-ioctl's check_fmt() rejected every OUTPUT buffer type with -EINVAL:
G_FMT failed before any of this driver's own code ran. Measured against
vivid's Video Output Multiplanar node (device_caps=0x05222000):

    queue type: OUTPUT_MPLANE
    FAIL G_FMT: Invalid argument

The board never hits it: bcm2835-codec is M2M, so it takes the first
branch and both directions work. That is why it went unnoticed -- and
it is what blocked exercising the output direction of the DMABUF path,
where the device model reads the guest pages instead of writing them.

Change-Id: I79f06852149002802ed2fbc4d82c3c3185dfc93d
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 driver/virtio_media_driver.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/driver/virtio_media_driver.c b/driver/virtio_media_driver.c
index 7fe98c4..1cd4783 100644
--- a/driver/virtio_media_driver.c
+++ b/driver/virtio_media_driver.c
@@ -912,7 +912,7 @@ static int virtio_media_probe(struct virtio_device *virtio_dev)
 	if (vd->device_caps & (V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_M2M | V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_M2M_MPLANE))
 		vd->vfl_dir = VFL_DIR_M2M;
 	else if (vd->device_caps &
-		 (V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_OUTPUT | V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE))
+		 (V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_OUTPUT | V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE))
 		vd->vfl_dir = VFL_DIR_TX;
 	else
 		vd->vfl_dir = VFL_DIR_RX;
